<speak>That's a fair observation. A clear title and a short first line can do more than a long explanation. When we arrange a call, you can also say if you expect to be travelling, so we don't contact you at an awkward local hour. You don't have to give a detailed itinerary. Just the practical availability is enough. For today's conversation, you seem comfortably settled, which is very different from trying to speak while walking through an airport or searching for a taxi.</speak>